          "note": "Computed from config.json for llama.cpp 3bb63cbcbfb62056c84fe9e521b0f3d756d29c32 (glm5-next): per token, each of the 11 deepseek_sparse_attention layers caches a K-only latent (kv_lora_rank 512 + qk_rope_head_dim 0) and a k-pool indexer row (3 × index_head_dim 128) at q8_0, 34/32 bytes: 11 × 896 × 34/32 = 10,472 bytes. Per conversation, whatever its length, each of the 34 linear_attention layers keeps one f32 state (short_conv_kernel_size 4, 64 heads × head_dim 128): 34 × (3 × 3 × 64 × 128 + 128 × 128 × 64) × 4 = 152,633,344 bytes. At 4 × 131,072 that is 5,818 MiB beside 185,437 MiB of weights on the GPU (the GGUF less its skipped MTP block and its CPU-side token embedding).",
